  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "How Low Should Your Kitchen Countertops Be?",
    "text": "How Low Should Your Kitchen Countertops Be?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Deciding on the right height for your kitchen countertops, especially for accessibility, is a crucial step in creating a truly functional space. There isn't a single universal answer, as the ideal height often depends on the specific user's needs and whether they'll be seated or standing. Generally, for seated users, a countertop height between 28 and 34 inches from the floor is common, allowing for comfortable access. However, it's not just about the top surface; you also need to consider the knee and toe clearance underneath. A minimum of 27 inches of clear height under the counter is often recommended, along with sufficient depth for knees and toes. You'll also need to decide if the lowered section will be a partial workstation or a continuous run. Coordinating sink or cooktop placement if they're also being lowered is essential, and make sure adjacent storage and outlets remain easily reachable. Getting the height right before fabrication is key, as modifications can be complex. If you're unsure about the optimal height for your specific situation or if the project involves structural changes, plumbing, or electrical work, a professional can provide invaluable guidance. HH Remodeling LLC, serving the greater Denver area, can help you customize your kitchen countertops to perfectly fit your needs.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
}